  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np25:2.10": "The six are linen, cotton, silk, wool, sunn hemp, and hemp; see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd8/en/brahmali#3.1.6'>Kd 8:3.1.6</a>.  According to <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-kd8/en/brahmali#21.1.4'>Kd 8:21.1.4</a>, the size referred to here  is no smaller than 8 by 4 <i lang='pi' translate='no'>sugataṅgula</i>, “standard fingerbreadths”. For an explanation of the idea of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>vikappanā</i>, see Appendix of Technical Terms. For the rendering of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>cīvara</i> as “robe-cloth”, see the same appendix. ",
